abstract: >
  A hybrid deep learning framework for monthly precipitation prediction in mountainous
  areas of Boyaca, Colombia. Provides reference implementations of eight model families
  and a uniform training, evaluation, and benchmarking pipeline: baseline ConvLSTM (with
  bidirectional, residual, and attention variants), Fourier Neural Operators (FNO and
  FNO-ConvLSTM hybrids), Graph Neural Networks with Temporal Attention (GNN-TAT, with
  GCN/GAT/GraphSAGE encoders), state-space (Mamba) variants, and a Late Fusion Ridge
  ensemble. Validated on the CHIRPS-SRTM dataset (61x65 grid, 518 monthly steps,
  1982-2025) with multi-seed evaluation across seeds {42, 123, 456}
  and lead times 1-12. Also implements AnchorBench v1.0, an evaluation protocol that
  anchors every architecture to zero-cost baselines, separates architectural effect
  from initialisation variance, decomposes ensemble gain into calibration and
  combination terms, tests deseasonalised anomaly skill, and diagnoses the learned
  spatial prior.
